    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 111.77,
      "end_seconds": 116.24,
      "duration_seconds": 4.47,
      "text": "what about your parents, brothers or sisters, any conditions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 117.99,
      "end_seconds": 121.71,
      "duration_seconds": 3.72,
      "text": "okay so my sister had breast cancer"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 130.62,
      "end_seconds": 133.35,
      "duration_seconds": 2.73,
      "text": "now some background about your lifestyle"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 134.81,
      "end_seconds": 154.95,
      "duration_seconds": 20.14,
      "text": "No, I've never smoked in my life. Nothing, I'm teetotal. I look after my grandchildren most days. I walk the dog every morning. I drink a lot of tea and snack through the day"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 155.8,
      "end_seconds": 158.53,
      "duration_seconds": 2.73,
      "text": "what's on your current medicine list?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 160.49,
      "end_seconds": 177.95,
      "duration_seconds": 17.46,
      "text": "Allopurinol. I take it 100 milligrams, once a day. Mm, uh, I take fluoxetine, 20 milligrams, every morning. I'm supposed to take it regularly, but I don't always manage"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 179.28,
      "end_seconds": 181.96,
      "duration_seconds": 2.68,
      "text": "Do you have any chronic illnesses?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 183.3,
      "end_seconds": 196.72,
      "duration_seconds": 13.42,
      "text": "I've had gout for about a year now i have depression, for nearly five years i just want to get back to normal, really"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 197.57,
      "end_seconds": 201.0,
      "duration_seconds": 3.43,
      "text": "I'll note down your vital signs first"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 208.41,
      "end_seconds": 210.84,
      "duration_seconds": 2.43,
      "text": "nearly done with the readings.."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 223.73,
      "end_seconds": 229.91,
      "duration_seconds": 6.18,
      "text": "Okay: BP is 113 over 75, heart rate 107, temperature is 36.6 degrees."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 231.41,
      "end_seconds": 234.75,
      "duration_seconds": 3.34,
      "text": "right, let's have a proper look at you"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 235.88,
      "end_seconds": 237.42,
      "duration_seconds": 1.54,
      "text": "fine by me"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 238.7,
      "end_seconds": 240.47,
      "duration_seconds": 1.77,
      "text": "alright, breathe out slowly"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 253.0,
      "end_seconds": 258.73,
      "duration_seconds": 5.73,
      "text": "Your tummy is tender low on the right and you look pale."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 261.13,
      "end_seconds": 263.01,
      "duration_seconds": 1.88,
      "text": "That's the examination finished."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 277.72,
      "end_seconds": 290.83,
      "duration_seconds": 13.11,
      "text": "Putting it all together it fits best with a possible ectopic pregnancy. The reason I say that is that your story and my examination fit together. Another possibility is a ruptured ovarian cyst."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 301.77,
      "end_seconds": 307.58,
      "duration_seconds": 5.81,
      "text": "A pregnancy test is what I'd like next, for pelvic pain and bleeding."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 313.28,
      "end_seconds": 316.3,
      "duration_seconds": 3.02,
      "text": "Do I need to prepare?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 318.2,
      "end_seconds": 324.11,
      "duration_seconds": 5.91,
      "text": "I think an urgent pelvic scan makes sense here, for possible ectopic."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 325.49,
      "end_seconds": 328.01,
      "duration_seconds": 2.52,
      "text": "Do I need to prepare?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 328.56,
      "end_seconds": 349.33,
      "duration_seconds": 20.77,
      "text": "you need to go to the hospital now for an emergency scan. Cut back on tea, coffee and fizzy drinks for a couple of weeks and see how things settle. I think the gynaecology team should see you too. That's everything on my side. Anything you're unsure about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 350.27,
      "end_seconds": 352.51,
